  "scope": "Independent mathematical review of UCE1-UCE9 and UCE18-UCE19, including the full exact same-g1 GdEnd consumer. UCE10-UCE17 have complementary independent review; no selected whole closure is proposed.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "topic": "Actual inertia separator and specialization in every characteristic",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "Read UCE1-UCE9 and UCE18-UCE19. The original GD condition ell-1 not dividing2e and the cyclotomic inertia image provide the actual unit separator. The field-specialization lemma uses a valuation ring dominating the supplied local domain, integral flag reduction, and a finite field extension from the finite polynomial equations. The ordered flag remains valid even when the coefficient uniformizer maps to zero."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Literal local ordinary condition",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "UCE3 derives the ordered product identities from the inherited all-Artin crystalline component, uses three diagonal projectors to force the inertia ordering, and proves decomposition-group stability by intertwining distinct characters. UCE4 uses integral spectral projectors to descend the ordered flag over the actual domain. UCE5 pushes all five OrdPt fields, including the original every-place away-inertia condition and the exact local embedding. No FinA or automorphy hypothesis is introduced."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Integral weights and full finite criterion",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "Actual entry deviations generate the relative cotangent space and the complete ring. Conjugation by T(1+T), universality and injectivity of Z to1+T modulo each maximal-ideal power prove homogeneous projection stability integrally, without dividing torus eigenvalue differences. Finite monomial generators give the complete local zero piece and finite fixed-weight modules. Projection proves R0 intersect pi R equals pi R0 even with pi-torsion."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Characteristic-prime curves and arbitrary original FinCrit tests",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "The prime maximal while avoiding a surviving element gives a one-dimensional quotient by principal ideal theorem and finite prime avoidance. Its finite residue field lifts inside the equal-characteristic complete domain; a nonzero parameter makes it finite over k[[t]]. The finite extension valuation yields an original complete DVR test with finite residue field and nonzero surviving element. The test kills every nonempty weight-zero monomial, so the zero piece is finite over O. Reducedness, coefficient flatness and characteristic-zero restrictions were not added."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Both conjugacy transports with all extension choices",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "TypeI is preserved by the actual torus conjugacy on ker eta. The same iota, cuspidal datum, infinity type, semisimplicity and cofinite Frobenius attachment transport through the cyclotomic twist. For TypeII the original four zero entries and middle-entry-one remain; every supplied full two-dimensional W is conjugated by diag(t,t^{-1}), keeping its corner equality and trace at the original complex conjugation. Its same newform attachment transports back after epsilon^{-e}. No preferred extension or quadratic twist was substituted."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Exact GdEnd consumer and explicit unclosed producer",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "Compared GdEnd, FinEnd, AutEnd3, AutEnd2, FinA, AutB, LemW and the entire AutomorphyUnramifiedCoefficients record. One invocation chooses the same g1 for the actual D, fixed iota and local valuation ring. Only then are U,S, arbitrary entry maps, pushed representations and every outer-corner extension varied. UCE10-UCE17 have complementary independent coverage, including finite weight zero, arbitrary entry-map ordinary realization and all-open-subgroup irreducibility. This proves the exact GdEnd implication but does not construct its finite-end or two automorphic-end fields. AUT_UNRAM_COEF stays open."
    }
  ],
